slipcase-common (1.0.0) stable; urgency=low

  * First release. The media type and its icon, taken out of the products that
    used to carry them so that one package owns them.
  * Breaks and Replaces slipcase-desktop before 0.1.3, which is where the icon
    moved out of. Without them dpkg refuses this package on any machine already
    carrying one of those versions.
  * The icon is declared twice in the media type, as the icon and as the
    generic icon. Without the second declaration a container draws as a blank
    generic document: GTK searches theme-major, and Adwaita answers
    application-x-generic before hicolor is reached.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sun, 31 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0000
